          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Avoid being the last player left with cards in your hand at the end of Phase Two.',
          gameplay: 'Phase 1: All players play one card to each trick; highest rank wins the trick. If there is a tie for highest, the tied players play again until the tie is broken. After each play, players draw from the stock to keep three cards until the stock is empty. The last card of the stock sets the trump suit for Phase 2. When the stock is exhausted, play continues without drawing until the player whose turn it is has no card to play; then Phase 2 begins. Phase 2: The holder of the trump card leads. You must either beat the previous card or sequence (higher same suit or any trump) or pick up the lowest card or sequence from the trick. The last player left with cards loses and is the Dog.',
          keyRules: [
            'Phase 1: All play one card per trick; no follow suit; highest rank wins; ties broken by replay.',
            'Phase 2: Trump from last card of stock; beat by higher same suit or any trump, or pick up lowest card or sequence from trick.',
            'Last player left with cards loses and is called the Dog.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "In Phase 1, try to win tricks with high cards of the same suit. This gives you 'runs' in Phase 2, which are very hard for opponents to beat (they must beat the whole run).",
          intermediate: "Hand Balancing: Don't win every trick in Phase 1. If you have too many cards in Phase 2, you are more likely to get stuck picking up even more.",
          advanced: 'The Sequence Trap: In Phase 2, if you have a sequence like 8-9-10 of Spades, wait until your opponent plays a low Spade. Then dump the entire sequence on them. They will likely have to pick it up, adding 3 cards to their hand.',
          tips: [
            "Keep track of the Aces during Phase 1. Knowing who has the 'Exit cards' for Phase 2 is vital.",
            'If you are leading in Phase 2, lead your middle-range cards first. Save your Aces for when you need to capture a trick to lead again.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
